# Local zsh overrides — deliberately not overwritten by chezmoi.
#
# Sourced last by ~/.zsh/rc.d/99-local.zsh, after every tracked fragment, so
# anything set here wins. The source file carries chezmoi's `create_` attribute:
# it is created on a fresh machine and then left alone forever, so local edits
# and installer appends survive `chezmoi apply`.
#
# Point installers that insist on editing a shell rc (pnpm, uv, bun, ...) at
# this file rather than ~/.zshrc, which chezmoi owns and will clobber. Anything
# that turns out to be permanent belongs back in the repo instead: ~/.zshenv for
# PATH and env vars needed by every shell, or a ~/.zsh/rc.d/ fragment for
# interactive-only setup.
